Watchmen is a 2024 American adult animated two-part superhero
film directed by Brandon Vietti and written by J.

10
00:38:10,909 --> 00:38:16,909
Michael Straczynski.

11
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
It stars an ensemble cast including Matthew Rhys, Katee Sackhoff, Titus
Welliver, Troy Baker, Adrienne Barbeau, and Michael Cerveris.

12
00:45:49,090 --> 00:45:55,090
Chapter I is the 57th film, and Chapter II is the 58th film of the DC
Universe Animated Original Movies, and produced by Warner Bros.

13
00:49:38,181 --> 00:49:44,181
Animation, Paramount Pictures, and DC
Entertainment, and distributed by Warner Bros.

14
00:53:27,272 --> 00:53:33,272
Home Entertainment in North America and Paramount Home Entertainment elsewhere.

15
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
The film is based on the DC Comics limited series of the same name co-created and illustrated by Dave Gibbons, with
co-creator and author Alan Moore choosing to remain uncredited here for his work on the source material.

16
01:01:05,454 --> 01:01:11,454
Set in an alternate 1985, the film follows a group of outlawed and retired superheroes
who investigate a conspiracy following the murder of one of their own.

17
01:04:54,545 --> 01:05:00,545
Gibbons served as a consulting producer on the film.

18
01:08:43,636 --> 01:08:49,636
Animation for the film was provided by Studio Mir.

19
01:12:32,727 --> 01:12:38,727
The first part (titled Watchmen Chapter I) was released on August 13, 2024, while the
second part (titled Watchmen Chapter II) was released on November 26, 2024.

20
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
The film explores themes of nuclear war, secret identity,
retirement, conspiracy, alternate history.

21
01:20:10,909 --> 01:20:16,909
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
